[TEXT] **Root cause found.** Router2 has explicit `iptables` FORWARD DROP rules targeting exactly the affected subnets — **not** a dead RIP daemon. The packet counter confirms these rules are actively hitting traffic.

```
FORWARD DROP  src 192.168.1.0/24 → any  (32 pkts dropped — IT dept)
FORWARD DROP  src 192.168.2.0/24 → any  (3  pkts dropped — CS dept)
```

This explains the asymmetry perfectly: office/principle (192.168.3.x, 192.168.4.x) are not listed in these rules and pass freely. RIP is healthy on all three routers with full routing tables.

